{"name":"Cumulus","hex":"#f3f3e6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cumulus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heap or mound.","A large white, puffy cloud that develops through convection."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cumulus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cumulus (software)","blocks":[{"text":"Cumulus is a digital asset management software designed for client/server system which is developed by Canto Software. The product makes use of metadata for indexing, organizing, and searching."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumulus_(software)"},{"title":"Cumulus cloud","blocks":[{"text":"Cumulus clouds are clouds that have flat bases and are often described as puffy, cotton-like, or fluffy in appearance. Their name derives from the Latin cumulus, meaning \"heap\" or \"pile\". Cumulus clouds are low-level clouds, generally less than 2,000 m (6,600 ft) in altitude unless they are the more vertical cumulus congestus form. Cumulus clouds may appear by themselves, in lines, or in clusters. They form due to condensation from oceans and lakes which rises up and cools from the colder atmosphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/GoldenMedows.jpg/330px-GoldenMedows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumulus_cloud"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Brittany_01.jpg/500px-Brittany_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Brittany_01.jpg/1280px-Brittany_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Brittany_01.jpg/500px-Brittany_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lines of cumulus clouds over Brittany, France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrittany_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Cumulusmediocrissweden.jpg/500px-Cumulusmediocrissweden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Cumulusmediocrissweden.jpg/500px-Cumulusmediocrissweden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cumulus mediocris clouds over Sweden","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACumulusmediocrissweden.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Anvil_of_Cumulonimbus_and_Cu_con.JPG/500px-Anvil_of_Cumulonimbus_and_Cu_con.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Anvil_of_Cumulonimbus_and_Cu_con.JPG/1280px-Anvil_of_Cumulonimbus_and_Cu_con.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Anvil_of_Cumulonimbus_and_Cu_con.JPG/500px-Anvil_of_Cumulonimbus_and_Cu_con.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cumulus congestus clouds compared against a cumulonimbus cloud in the background","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnvil_of_Cumulonimbus_and_Cu_con.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Cirrocumulus_in_Hong_Kong.jpg/500px-Cirrocumulus_in_Hong_Kong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Cirrocumulus_in_Hong_Kong.jpg/1280px-Cirrocumulus_in_Hong_Kong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Cirrocumulus_in_Hong_Kong.jpg/500px-Cirrocumulus_in_Hong_Kong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A large f